  "page1": {
    "title": "Walking in Others' Shoes",
    "subtitle": "Learn to feel what your friends feel, and treat them with care.",
    "body": "Mina sat alone at lunch. She looked sad and quiet. Her friend Jun saw her face.\n\nJun did not laugh at her. He sat down next to Mina. \"Are you okay?\" he asked softly.\n\nMy mom says we should <mark>walk in someone's shoes</mark>. This does not mean we take their shoes. It means we try to feel what they feel.\n\nThis is called <u>empathy</u>. When we have empathy, we care about other people.\n\nJun showed care for Mina. He did not know her whole story. But he still tried to understand her.\n\nMina felt better. A small act of care can warm a heart. When we respect others, they feel safe with us.\n\nCare and respect make us good friends.",
    "illustration": "assets/illustrations/mars/2026-07/09.jpg",
    "illustration_caption": "Jun sits beside a sad Mina at lunch, asking softly if she is okay."
  },
